  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a peer-reviewed tomography picker address automation, reconstruction, and density validation in cryo-EM workflows.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational refinement of macromolecular density data, in which sequential or manual processing and interpretation steps are being replaced by integrated, automated, or statistically defined procedures. CryoPilot uses two LLM agents to adaptively select CryoSPARC jobs and validate models across nine public datasets. End2EndPtychoSPA fits a 3D potential and particle poses directly to 4D-STEM data through a differentiable multislice model, improving resolution over sequential reconstruction. Astex-Faro applies a reference-ensemble statistical framework with a new FSCoh consistency metric to flag significant density deviations in cryo-EM maps. RobPicker addresses label noise and rare-species reweighting to improve macromolecule particle picking in cryo-ET tomograms. FoXSight and PHENOMS are adjacent computational tools, addressing crystallographic fragment screening and MD hydrogen-bond analysis respectively, and are included here for their methodological overlap rather than shared experimental context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
